title: Fundraising
subtitle: Money wins campaigns, and costs us something.
tags: party_action
new-page: true
view-if: fundraise_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; fundraise_timer = 1

= Fundraising

The party needs money for field offices, ads, and voter protection. The question is whose money.

- @small_dollar: Build a small-dollar machine.
- @megadonors: Court the megadonors.
- @pac: Coordinate with outside groups and PACs.

@small_dollar
subtitle: +2 funds, base enthusiasm up. Slow and steady.
on-arrival: funds += 2; enthusiasm += 3; prog_dissent -= 3; estab_dissent += 1

Email lists, text-to-donate, and a thousand house parties. It is not glamorous, but it ties the base to the party.

@megadonors
subtitle: +4 funds, but the base grumbles.
on-arrival: funds += 4; enthusiasm -= 2; prog_dissent += 4; far_left += 1; mod_dissent -= 2

The big checks arrive fast. So do the headlines about who wrote them.

@pac
subtitle: +3 funds and a bit of media reach, at some cost in control.
on-arrival: funds += 3; media_trust += 1; unity -= 1

Coordinated spending stretches every dollar, but the message gets harder to control.
